<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rurik dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">862–<a href="/years/1598">1598</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Rurikids</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rurikids were the ruling dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kievan-rus">Kievan Rus'</a> and its successor principalities, traditionally descended from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rurik">Rurik</a>, a Varangian said to have settled at Novgorod around 862. Princes of the family shared out the towns of Rus' among themselves, and its branches ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kyiv</a>, Galicia-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volhynia">Volhynia</a>, Vladimir and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>. The Muscovite line ended with the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsar">Tsar</a> Feodor I in 1598.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rurik-dynasty.jpg" alt="Rurik dynasty" width="320" height="335" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vladimir Lobachev · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coin_of_Yaroslav_the_Wise_(reverse).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Kievan Rus' was the first great state of the East Slavs, a federation of <b>Rurikid</b> principalities on the Dnieper trade route whose adoption of Byzantine Orthodoxy around 988 shaped the religion, writing and culture of eastern Europe, and from which Ukraine, Belarus and Russia all trace their origins.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kievan-rus">Kievan Rus' · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>In the 1080s three <b>Rurikid</b> brothers, Rurik, Volodar and Vasylko Rostislavich, took control of the towns of Peremyshl, Zvenyhorod and Terebovl in the far south-west of Rus'.</blockquote><a href="/state/principality-of-galicia">Principality of Galicia</a></li></ul></section>
